SUMMARY:Behind Broadway: A Performance with Lorna Courtney 
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: $50.00 per person\nAvailability: 49 
 spots left\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinh
 ouse.com/events/208796\n\n5:00PM Doors Open\, 5:15PM Performance\, 6:00PM 
 Reception\nJoin us in The Reading Room for an intimate evening of music\, 
 theatre\, and storytelling with Tony Award-nominated Broadway star Lorna C
 ourtney. Best known for originating the role of Juliet in the hit musical 
 “& Juliet”\, Courtney brings her extraordinary talent to The ’Quin f
 or a captivating live performance featuring selections from across her car
 eer\, from her early days on Broadway to her celebrated roles in “Heathe
 rs: The Musical” and “The Rocky Horror Picture Show”. Through song a
 nd personal storytelling\, Courtney will take members on a journey through
  the defining performances\, inspirations\, and experiences that have shap
 ed her career on the stage.\n\nFollowing the 30 minute performance\, Court
 ney will be joined for an engaging conversation and Q&A with Artistic Dire
 ctor of SpeakEasy Stage Company\, Dawn Simmons. Together\, the two will of
 fer a behind-the-curtain look at the world of Broadway\, exploring the cre
 ative process\, pivotal career moments\, and the evolving landscape of mus
 ical theatre while members enjoy light bites.\n\n*Tickets are $50 per mem
 ber and $75 for one registered guest. All tickets are nonrefundable and no
 ntransferable. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208796
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
