SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Georgia" by Dawn Tripp 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 14 spots left\nS
 tatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20878
 9\n\nBookmark your calendar and settle in for November’s Author Circle B
 ook Club\, Georgia by Dawn Tripp—a captivating and richly imagined novel
  inspired by the extraordinary life of iconic American artist Georgia O’
 Keeffe.\n\nSet against the vibrant art world of early 20th-century New Yor
 k and the striking landscapes of New Mexico\, Georgia explores the woman b
 ehind the art\, tracing her passionate pursuit of independence\, creativit
 y\, and love. Through her complex relationship with photographer Alfred St
 ieglitz and her determination to forge a path entirely her own\, Tripp pai
 nts an intimate portrait of ambition\, identity\, and artistic expression.
  A beautifully layered story sure to inspire thoughtful conversation.\n\n*
 This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary l
 ight bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancel
 lations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208789
CATEGORIES:The Arts
